# ============================================================
# How it works — examples
# ============================================================
#
# When a PR modifies /proxy/main.go:
#   → matched by /proxy/main.go → @gasciljh assigned.
#
# When a PR modifies /install_app.sh (v1.5.0):
#   → matched by /install_app.sh → @gasciljh assigned.
#   → Reviewer MUST verify:
#       • 5 cascade levels intact
#       • 75-second deadline present
#       • Three-way trap split (EXIT/INT/TERM, 130/143)
#       • SELinux staging still uses /data/local/tmp/
#       • No `setenforce 0`
#       • Play Protect trap restores `$_VERIFIER_ORIG`
#     See SECURITY.md §5.36 and docs/REFERENCE.md §3.13.
#
# When a PR modifies /lib/constants.sh (v1.6.0):
#   → matched by /lib/constants.sh → @gasciljh assigned.
#   → Reviewer MUST verify:
#       • _MONITORING_UI_PORT is still the canonical definition
#         (no duplicate in boot-mini.sh beyond §[4] fallback)
#       • No other Layer-0 primitive moved here without
#         updating boot-mini.sh and ci.yml Step 9
#
# When a PR modifies /boot-mini.sh (v1.6.0):
#   → matched by /boot-mini.sh → @gasciljh assigned.
#   → Reviewer MUST verify:
#       • The file remains an aggregator only (no business logic)
#       • All 6 lib/*.sh modules are still sourced in order
#       • The 5 primitives + _MONITORING_UI_PORT fallback (§[4])
#         are intact
#       • functions.sh still sources boot-mini.sh (no redefinition)
#     CI Step 9 in ci.yml catches regressions automatically.
#
# When a PR modifies /proxy/go.mod or /proxy/go.sum:
#   → A new external dependency requires its own ADR
#     (ADR-0002 compliance rule).
#
# When a PR modifies docs/REFERENCE.md §7 (manifest x-note fields):
#   → Reviewer MUST verify that every `x-note-*` field extracted
#     from web/manifest.json is still documented here.
#
# When a PR modifies /.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml:
#   → Reviewer MUST verify that any new `exclude:` block has a
#     documented rationale and that no `go/path-injection` or
#     `go/command-injection` rule is suppressed.
#
